    "note": "Presenting complaint:\nRight-sided throbbing headaches for 2 weeks.\n\nHistory:\nPain 6 to 8 out of 10, associated with photophobia, nausea and visual aura (zigzag lines). No vomiting, weakness or numbness. Screen use worsens symptoms. Taking ibuprofen 400 mg four times a week with partial relief. Caffeine intake 3 cups a day.\n\nPast medical history: Nil.\nFamily history: Sister with migraines. Father had a stroke at 70.\n\nExamination:\nFundoscopy normal. Cranial nerves intact. No focal neurological deficit. No neck stiffness. Blood pressure normal.\n\nImpression:\nMigraine with aura, possible medication overuse headache.\n\nPlan:\nHeadache diary for one month. Reassured regarding tumour concerns."
